@auth.sigil from Auth import { identity and access, renter }
@resource-management.sigil from ResourceManagement import { base availability rules }

component SchedulingAndRecurrence {
    goal {
        Manages each *recurring booking pattern* and resulting
        *recurring booking series* so a renter can request repeating room bookings
        without creating each occurrence separately.
    }

    interface {
        A recurring booking pattern describes a local start time, duration,
        recurrence rule, and date range.

        Scheduling and Recurrence expands a valid recurring booking pattern into a
        recurring booking series of dated occurrences.

        A user can add a *series exception* to skip or move one occurrence without
        changing the other occurrences in that series.

        Expanding a local-time pattern across clock changes requires
        *regional time-zone rules*.
    }

    state {
        Scheduling and Recurrence owns the recurring booking pattern,
        recurring booking series, and series exception.

        A recurring booking series links one pattern to its dated occurrences.

        A series exception applies to one occurrence in its recurring booking series.
    }

    logic {
        Scheduling and Recurrence validates a requested recurring booking pattern.
        If it is rejected, the module returns a validation result and ends that path.

        For an accepted recurring booking pattern, Scheduling and Recurrence expands
        it into dated occurrences in a recurring booking series.

        Scheduling and Recurrence applies each series exception to the matching
        dated occurrence to produce the adjusted occurrence set.

        Scheduling and Recurrence returns the recurring booking series containing
        the accepted pattern and adjusted occurrence set.

        Separately, it builds a *series-date preview* from the recurring booking
        pattern for the booking form.
    }

    constraints {
        base availability rules remain owned by Resource Management. Expanding a
        series does not decide whether its occurrences are bookable for a room.

        identity and access decides whether a user may create or change a recurring
        booking series; Scheduling and Recurrence does not own users, sessions, roles,
        or permission policy.

        For a recurring booking series, modules exchange contracts and do not read
        another module's private storage or logic.
    }

    cases {
        A renter requests a weekly recurring booking pattern across four weeks and
        adds a series exception to skip one date; only that occurrence is omitted
        from the recurring booking series.
    }
}
